Explanation:

The principal logarithm is defined by $"Log"(z) = ln|z| + i "Arg"(z)$ where $-pi < "Arg"(z) <= pi$.
For $z = 1 + i$:
$ |z| = sqrt(1^2 + 1^2) = sqrt(2) = 2^(1/2) $
$ "Arg"(z) = arctan(1 / 1) = pi / 4 $
Therefore:
$ "Log"(1 + i) = ln(2^(1/2)) + i pi / 4 = 1/2 ln 2 + i pi / 4 = (ln 2) / 2 + i pi / 4. $
